Description: Resolve compiler wide char size in conditional directives
Subject: Resolve compilerwidechar size without directive sizeof
License: expat

FPC 2.6.0 defines `tcompilerwidechar = word' in compiler/widestr.pas, so
`sizeof(tcompilerwidechar)' is 2 in these directive tests.  Replace the type
size checks with explicit numeric comparisons instead of teaching p2cc's lexer
about compiler type sizes.

--- a/compiler/ncon.pas
+++ b/compiler/ncon.pas
@@ -840,10 +840,10 @@
             { don't use getdata, because the compilerwidechars may have to
               be byteswapped
             }
-{$if sizeof(tcompilerwidechar) = 2}
+{$if 1 = 1}
             for i:=0 to pw^.len-1 do
               pw^.data[i]:=ppufile.getword;
-{$elseif sizeof(tcompilerwidechar) = 4}
+{$elseif 1 = 0}
             for i:=0 to pw^.len-1 do
               pw^.data[i]:=cardinal(ppufile.getlongint);
 {$else}
--- a/compiler/symsym.pas
+++ b/compiler/symsym.pas
@@ -1668,10 +1668,10 @@
                { don't use getdata, because the compilerwidechars may have to
                  be byteswapped
                }
-{$if sizeof(tcompilerwidechar) = 2}
+{$if 1 = 1}
                for i:=0 to pw^.len-1 do
                  pw^.data[i]:=ppufile.getword;
-{$elseif sizeof(tcompilerwidechar) = 4}
+{$elseif 1 = 0}
                for i:=0 to pw^.len-1 do
                  pw^.data[i]:=cardinal(ppufile.getlongint);
 {$else}
